    "author": "Test Forecaster A",
    "status": "published",
    "product_type": "forecast",
    "bottom_line": "<p>Sun and warm temperatures will cause loose avalanches on steep slopes once the snow surface becomes moist or wet. Dry slab avalanches are also possible on steep, upper-elevation slopes where wind has formed thick drifts and slabs. You can reduce your risk by choosing slopes that face away from the sun, where the snow is more likely to remain soft and dry.</p>\n<p><em>Today is our last daily Avalanche Forecast of the season. We will issue General Avalanche Information updates through late April or early May. Thanks for the great season, everyone.&nbsp;</em></p>",
